{"id": "EUVD-2026-103514", "enisaUuid": "ae8e0c49-b435-3458-8c8b-66b0ef961add", "description": "libspatialite through 5.1.0 contains an integer overflow vulnerability in the WKB point and vertex count size guard of ParseWkbLine and related parsers in gg_wkb.c, allowing out-of-bounds reads. Attackers can supply a crafted geometry BLOB with a large point count, for example in a SpatiaLite database file, to crash the process or corrupt heap memory on 32-bit builds.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T12:19:43", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T18:01:10", "baseScore": 6.9, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:N/VI:L/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@haindpwn/libspatialite-wkb-geometry-count-overflow", "https://www.gaia-gis.it/fossil/libspatialite/file?name=src/gaiageo/gg_wkb.c&ci=5a5528e8d2", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/libspatialite-through-5.1.0-integer-overflow-in-wkb-geometry-parsing"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-112052", "GHSA-8jmj-j7pf-v8j3"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.12, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "780062ea-1cd5-385c-a981-ad0d8177e555", "product": {"name": "libspatialite", "vendor": {"name": "SpatiaLite"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22645.1.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "33fbc432-d784-3d65-99dd-2fd56a3b9f5b", "vendor": {"name": "SpatiaLite"}}], "isExploited": false}